# Agent lessons

**First action on every coding task:** `Read` [`docs/auxiliary/engineering/AGENT_LESSONS.md`](../../docs/auxiliary/engineering/AGENT_LESSONS.md) before editing solvers, Study/desktop, Zig host, or docs that claim product behavior. Do not skip. Root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) repeats this requirement. Refresh playbook: [`docs/auxiliary/engineering/AGENT_LESSONS_REFRESH.md`](../../docs/auxiliary/engineering/AGENT_LESSONS_REFRESH.md).

**Parallel work**

- Assume siblings may write into `/workspace` even when asked to use a worktree. Do not checkout/commit there while they run unless ownership is proven disjoint.
- Give each agent a disjoint path list. Serialize `build.zig`, `tauri.conf.json`, `solver_engine.rs`, `host/src/dispatch.zig`, and `desktop/src/engine/{client,transport}.ts`, or have only the parent touch them.
- Subagents often cannot `ManagePullRequest`; the parent opens PRs after push and subscribes CI.
- If the tree is interleaved: WIP snapshot branch, then path-checkout onto clean `cursor/<feature>-<run-suffix>` branches from the product tip (`main`).
- Re-run `git status` immediately before every commit; restore unexpected paths.
- Follow-ups committed on an already-merged PR head never reach the base — rebase onto the correct tip as a new PR.

**Architecture / Study correctness (short)**

- On `main`, Study ships Zig `solver-engine` typed IPC. Do not add an HTTP solve server or a second engine binary.
- Live river-beta (`?river-beta=1` + `services/river-beta/`) ≠ public demo Pages ≠ Tauri desktop. Do not arm river-beta in public-demo builds; reconnect on reaped/`no_session` sessions.
- Windows: GUI subsystem + `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` for `solver-engine`; pin `-Dcpu=x86_64_v2`; drain stderr on spawn. Startup console flashes are often LocalDumps `reg.exe` without `CREATE_NO_WINDOW`, not the sidecar.
- Tauri IPC: demux by `request_id`; Rust owns the connection async (no sync command blocking the UI thread on pipe I/O); bounded admission with control priority; typed fail-once recovery on connection loss. Don't hold the lifecycle mutex for the whole RPC; don't kill train on one timeout. Cap train threads so IPC stdin is not CPU-starved; never free GiB trees under `session.mu`; soft status timeouts and queue saturation during Building/Solving are congestion backoff, not a hung kill. Stop/Pause are job-scoped: match `active_job_id`; never `requestStop` for a stale/unknown job id. Hung kill is launch-scoped (`expected_launch_id`). Analysis is one persistent worker with a generation per metric (a `values` call does not cancel `node`); return budget only for the live generation. Compare parks joinable orphans (never detach). Build, Open, Save, and train share one exclusive mutation gate; Status and cancel stay available. Protocol-2 payload ceiling is 16 MiB. Parent stdin EOF stops, joins workers, then re-asserts stop. On x86_64, `zig build` defaults to `x86_64_v2`; `-Dcpu=native` can emit AVX-512.
- Prefer root-cause (IPC headroom, job/launch scope, async Rust boundary) over timeout bumps, retries, or UI masking. Zig host smokes ≠ Tauri UI-thread concurrency — packaged Windows WebView gates are required for those claims.
- Nash gap is NashConv (sum of BR gains). Accuracy / stop criterion is Pio’s average (NashConv/2). Host `solve` uses a pot fraction. The Build Accuracy field is percent of pot (`0.5` = engine `0.005`). Compare stop thresholds to Accuracy chips, not raw NashConv. Study chrome is dark-only. The Study page is node nav, matrix, and a permanent right rail. Solve controls are in the status bar. The equity dock tab is Equity.
- Own-reach averaging; CF regret uses opponent×chance; tiny compatible mass must not invent a uniform opponent; Equity is check-down pot fraction ≠ chip EV.
- Study node equity must be reach-weighted at the selected node; Equity Calculator jobs are a separate IPC surface. Local EV: `local_offset` + Fold from `values.actions`.
- Wide-range flop EV/equity “never loads”: root `values` must use threaded frozen first-card walk (WorkerBudget analysis borrow); equity pair-runout preflight is O(n0·n1) closed-form + runout-outer ranks — never nest runouts in the count; do not prefetch non-root flop/turn child `/values` (deal-by-deal saturates the single analysis worker). Post-solve: reuse Session warm FrozenCtx ranks (`acquireFrozenCtxForAnalysis` + OnCtx values/equity) — do not rebuild rank caches per request. Starting-board facing (Root x) `values` must also use that warm path with path-conditioned reach — not deal-by-deal. Warm equity WorkLimit is hand×runout (`study_warm_max_hand_runouts`), not the pair-runout ceiling; After Call must reuse that warm path. Not an IPC timeout bump.
- Heap-stable runout ranks under MT; train freeze must apply locks; frozen-root aev reports `Q_i`.
- Street config is `street-config 1` text. A missing or empty bet list is check-only. There is no `{0.5, 1}` default. Raise lists do not copy bets. No Flop donk control. Preview/plan-memory must not mutate Session.
- Shipped trainer is CFR+. PSOL v4 stores that algorithm byte only. Settings shows CFR+ only. The host trains CFR+.
- AI packs: edit `docs/ai-context/source/` then `npm run sync:ai-context` / CI `check:ai-context`. Do not hand-edit generated packs.
- Do not change `LICENSE`. Update `docs/auxiliary/planning/FEATURE_PARITY.md` only with the commit that demonstrates the row.
